          "id": "Measure 26-267",
          "title": "Amends Charter: Portland residents decide 2% of city's annual discretionary budget.",
          "summary": "Amends the Portland City Charter to require City Council to set aside an amount equal to at least 2% of the city's General Fund discretionary ongoing expenses for a participatory budgeting program, starting July 2027. Any resident could propose citywide or district projects; city staff and budget delegates from all districts would narrow them to feasible projects, and residents would then make binding selections. The official estimate is about $16.4 million in fiscal year 2027-28 and $17.0 million in 2028-29.",
          "yesMeans": "Portland residents would decide through a binding participatory process how to spend at least 2% of the city's discretionary budget.",
          "noMeans": "The current budget process, in which the Mayor proposes and Council amends and adopts the budget, would not change.",
